# Utopia Sprawl is on Bot1's Forest when Consecrate Land arrives on it: the Sprawl is put into its owner's graveyard (the
# 2006 ruling; CR 303.4, 704.5m) and the Consecrate Land stays. Bot2 can still cast its own Utopia Sprawl targeting the Forest
# (CR 303.4a: only its enchant ability defines its targets) - it is on the stack, then goes to Bot2's graveyard instead of
# entering (CR 303.4i). Bot1's second Consecrate Land is "another Aura": it too is cast targeting the Forest, resolves and
# goes to the graveyard instead of entering, and the first stays. Only the enchanted land is indestructible: Bot1's Plains
# is not.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Mox Pearl
Utopia Sprawl
Consecrate Land
Consecrate Land
Plains
Plains
Plains x25

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Emerald
Utopia Sprawl
Island x30

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Hand.Utopia Sprawl.Cast(Forest)
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Colors(Red)
? Bot1.Battlefield.Utopia Sprawl.AttachedTo = Forest
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Consecrate Land.Cast(Forest)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
? Bot1.Graveyard = Utopia Sprawl
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Utopia Sprawl.Cast(Bot1.Battlefield.Forest)
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
? Bot2.Graveyard = Utopia Sprawl
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Consecrate Land.Cast(Forest)
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Graveyard = Consecrate Land; Utopia Sprawl
Bot1.Battlefield.Consecrate Land.AttachedTo = Forest
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Keywords = Indestructible
Bot1.Battlefield.Plains.Keywords = (absent)
Bot2.Graveyard = Utopia Sprawl
Bot2.Battlefield = Mox Emerald
